        "parms": "# makenote — notes that end by themselves\nmakenote turns a pitch into a complete note: it sends the pitch with a velocity at once, and the same pitch with velocity 0, the release, a duration later. Its arguments are the starting velocity and the duration in milliseconds: makenote 100 200 plays at velocity 100 for 200 ms. The velocity and duration inlets set them for the notes that follow, and send nothing. The velocity goes out before the pitch, so the pitch is the value that plays the note.\nMax's makenote also takes note values such as 4n as a duration, and a third argument gives it a channel inlet and outlet. Here the duration is in milliseconds only, and the channel belongs to the object that sends the note, such as noteon.",
